Apple is aiming to get people to sign up for the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-card/">Apple Card</a> over the holidays by offering a 2X Daily Cash bonus for new users.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2023/06/Apple-Card-Balance.jpeg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-898056" /><br/>
iPhone users who <a href="https://learn.applecard.apple/double-your-daily-cash-promo">sign up for an Apple Card</a> by December 10 can earn up to six percent Daily Cash on purchases for the first year after opening the account, with Apple offering up to &#36;1,000 total bonus Daily Cash.<br/>
<br/>
The promo doubles the standard Daily Cash back rewards:<br/>
<ul><br/>
 	<li><strong>6%</strong> - At Apple and participating merchants when using &zwnj;Apple Card&zwnj; with <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-pay/">Apple Pay</a>.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>4%</strong> - On purchases made using an &zwnj;Apple Card&zwnj; with &zwnj;Apple Pay&zwnj;.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>2%</strong> - On purchases made with the physical &zwnj;Apple Card&zwnj; or virtual card number (no &zwnj;Apple Pay&zwnj;).</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
After a year or when the &#36;1,000 bonus Daily Cash limit is reached, Daily Cash will revert to the standard one, two, and three percent rewards. Getting the full bonus amount would require spending about &#36;33,333 at six percent, &#36;50,000 at four percent, or &#36;100,000 at two percent, so for many users, the bonus cash earned will be less than Apple's maximum.<br/>
<br/>
Those interested in the deal will need to <a href="https://learn.applecard.apple/double-your-daily-cash-promo">apply through the promo website</a>, as Apple says the deal may not be available elsewhere. The promotion is not available to current &zwnj;Apple Card&zwnj; holders or those who have had an &zwnj;Apple Card&zwnj; in the past.<br/>
